WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.888
But in the same way our visions inspire&nbsp;us,

00:00:02.888 --> 00:00:05.391
they can also start to limit us.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:09.171
If we hear the same narratives
 over and over&nbsp;again,

00:00:09.171 --> 00:00:12.934
and if we see the same&nbsp;
visuals over and over again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:17.254
then that becomes our scope of possibility.

00:00:17.254 --> 00:00:21.640
That becomes our benchmark for 
what we believe is good and what's not.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:25.888
Talk to your grandmother asked 
her how she imagines the future,

00:00:25.888 --> 00:00:29.146
and I bet you&nbsp;she'll tell you that
 no one asks her that anymore

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:35.880
or read that Filipino science fiction novel,&nbsp;
watch a Nigerian, post apocalyptic film.&nbsp;

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:39.321
Look for stories that ask what
if from a new&nbsp;perspective,

00:00:39.321 --> 00:00:42.576
when we choose to be curious 
about the alternatives and

00:00:42.576 --> 00:00:44.858
when we take them seriously,

00:00:45.452 --> 00:00:47.872
we'll start to think in new ways,

00:00:47.872 --> 00:00:50.467
will solve problems in new ways,

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:53.762
and we'll just start to&nbsp;see possibilities
that we couldn't see before.

